# Glow Color System

This document defines the Glow brand color system and semantic colors used throughout the application.

## Brand Colors

### Core Palette

- **Glow Black**: `#050505` - Primary text and dark elements
- **Glow White**: `#ffffff` - Primary background and light elements
- **Glow Light Grey**: `#fafafa` - Subtle backgrounds
- **Glow Medium Grey**: `#f3f3f3` - Borders and dividers

### Accent Colors

- **Glow Orange**: `#ffb472` - Accent color for CTAs and highlights
- **Glow Yellow**: `#f7fcc4` - Gradient component
- **Glow Green**: `#ccffd4` - Gradient component, success states
- **Glow Purple**: `#dcc4ff` / `#d792ff` - Gradient component, delegation

## Semantic Colors

### Protocol Role Colors

#### Miner Color

- **Miner Blue**: `#2081e2` (OpenSea Sea Blue)
  - CSS Variable: `--color-miner`
  - Contrast Variant: `--color-miner-contrast` (same as base for now)
  - Used for: Miner badges, miner-related UI elements, mining center indicators
  - Usage: Backgrounds (with opacity), borders, text, icons

#### Delegation Color

- **Delegation Purple**: `#a855f7` (light mode) / `#d792ff` (dark mode)
  - CSS Variable: `--delegation-purple`
  - Used for: Delegation badges, delegation-related UI elements

## Migration Notes

### Miner Color Update (Jan 2026)

The miner color was changed from yellow (`#d9f368`) to a modern blue (`#2081e2`, inspired by OpenSea's Sea Blue) to better distinguish miners from other protocol elements and improve visual hierarchy. This vibrant blue provides a contemporary look while maintaining excellent contrast. All references should use the CSS variable `--color-miner` or `--color-miner-contrast` for easy future updates.

## Usage Guidelines

### Using Color Variables

Always reference colors through CSS variables rather than hard-coding hex values:

```css
/* Good */
.miner-badge {
  color: var(--color-miner-contrast);
  background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-miner) 10%, transparent);
  border-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-miner) 30%, transparent);
}

/* Bad */
.miner-badge {
  color: #1c4fc9;
  background-color: rgba(28, 79, 201, 0.1);
}
```

### Tailwind Usage

Use the CSS variable classes:

```tsx
// Good
<div className="text-[color:var(--color-miner-contrast)]" />
<div className="bg-[color:var(--color-miner)]/10" />
<div className="border-[color:var(--color-miner)]/30" />

// Avoid
<div className="text-miner-yellow" /> // Old class, deprecated
```

## Color Contrast Requirements

All text colors must meet WCAG AA standards:

- Normal text: minimum 4.5:1 contrast ratio
- Large text: minimum 3:1 contrast ratio
- Interactive elements: minimum 3:1 contrast ratio

The miner blue (`#2081e2`, OpenSea Sea Blue) provides excellent contrast on white backgrounds and works well with opacity adjustments for borders and backgrounds. This vibrant shade creates a modern, professional appearance while maintaining WCAG AA accessibility standards.
